WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.602
-I think this is
a very exciting time to have you

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
less than a week
before midterm elections.

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've been out
promoting this film.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've been urging people
to vote.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yes.
And I've been working

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:13.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
for candidates and,
at the same time,

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:13.813 size:78% position:39% line:92%
yes, the film is out.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:16.583
Actually, I had to go to Europe
to open it over there.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:18.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
Get back here
to help the election.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:22.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I've been
so busy, actually --

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:23.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna be on the road
next weekend.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
I won't be home
in Michigan to vote,

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my absentee ballot
just arrived

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.362 line:92%
just before I came down here.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:33.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, if you don't mind,
could I just vote?

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, do you want to vote
right now?

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.836 size:84% position:42%
You want to show people
how easy it is to vote?

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.338 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.440 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-This is the actual --

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
the actual ballot
for the state of Michigan.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:44.210 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Thank you very much.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And have you done --
You've done all your research?

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:47.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Oh, yeah.
-Okay.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:50.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I -- I know everybody
on this ballot.

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:52.285 line:92%
-You know everybody, yes.

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:55.555
-So, uh, I'm gonna vote for
Gretchen there for governor.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-And, you know,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
there are so many women
on the ballot.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:01.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
You'll notice this
when you go to vote next week.

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:06.266 size:81% position:41%
Just teachers alone,
there are 550 teachers

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:06.900 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
across the country

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are running
for state house or state rep.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:12.939 size:88% position:44%
-That's really exciting.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:13.873 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It'S an amazing --

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
While you're voting,
I want to say that you --

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the things
you talk about in the film

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:21.748
is how the biggest block of
voters are those who don't vote.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:22.515 size:84% position:42% line:92%
More people didn't vote

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.150 size:78% position:39%
than voted for either
of the candidates.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:27.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's our largest political
party, the non-voters.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.121 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Sad -- Sad to say.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:28.955 line:92%
-So how do you encourage those?

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is the message
you give to the non-voters

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:32.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get them out the door
this coming Tuesday?

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:35.662
-The thing I -- The thing
I say to non-voters is,

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:39.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
actually, I don't think
it works to, like, shame them

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.800 line:92%
or wag your finger at them.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think you should
listen to them

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:44.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
and find out
why they're not voting.

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:47.474
I'm guessing most people
that don't vote, that stay home,

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:50.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
do it because they're just --
they've given up,

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.045 line:92%
the system has failed them.

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:54.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
They don't see any difference
between the candidates.

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.483 line:92%
It's the same old hacks running.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:57.217 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And so, they stay home.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:02:01.254
But I'm gonna guess that
the majority of non-voters

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:05.492
deeply love their country
and are deeply patriotic.

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:07.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's got to be
very hard for them, Seth,

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:10.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
to stay home
and not participate.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think
they'd love to participate.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:13.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so what I say to them
this year is,

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.070 size:88% position:44%
there are so many people
on the ballot this time

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.271 line:92%
that are not the party hacks.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:21.374 size:84% position:42%
I mean, there's a --
There's a woman running

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:25.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
for Congress in West Virginia,
who she's a chicken farmer.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:28.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a bus driver,
I think it's in Kentucky,

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:28.948 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that's running.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:33.753
There's a librarian where I live
that's running.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.221 line:92%
I mean, these are, like --

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.356 line:92%
You know, there's a lunch lady

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's running somewhere
out in the Northwest,

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:39.526 line:92%
that's running for office.

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:44.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, like, normal people
are running this time.

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.098 size:88% position:44% line:92%
A lot of them are women.

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.232 line:92%
A lot of them are young people.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:50.336
And I think my -- if any
non-voter is watching this,

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd say give it a shot
just this one time.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.040 line:92%
Show up just this one time.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think you'll be surprised
by who's on the ballot.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we can throw
all the bastards out.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
-That's why --

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:02.982 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:03.583 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Now --

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:07.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh.
Prop 1 in Michigan.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Legalizing marijuana.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:11.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, are you on the fence
on this one?

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, do you want to help me
fill this one in?

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It looks like
it came filled in.

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:16.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ] Yeah!
-Yeah.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:17.964 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The band
wanted to vote on this.

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:20.333 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, no.
This is all my voting.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:22.969
Only I have touched this ballot.
-All right, good.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:25.038
-'Cause they're watching
in Michigan, and they'll --

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:25.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-There we go.

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:28.208
Thank you for letting me vote.
-So I want to ask about this.

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:31.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were here right before
the 2016 election.

00:03:31.678 --> 00:03:32.745 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And you --

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.881
Because, again, there's
this predicted blue wave.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.649 size:88% position:44%
You were very cautious
going into the election.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.785
You actually believed that
Donald Trump was gonna win.

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:41.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
You called it --
You called it state by state.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
So now
I'm give you another chance --

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.390 line:92%
how do you feel about Tuesday?

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:48.127
-Well, I'm not gonna make the
mistake that someone else made

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:50.997 size:75% position:38%
on a late-night show
a couple nights ago.

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:51.664 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:52.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A Democrat.
-Yes.

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:55.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who just automatically
announced, "We're gonna win."

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:56.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-And it's like,

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
"My God, that's what happened
in 2016."

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:03.476
Everybody was throwing the party
for Hillary before the election.

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:05.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think
some people stayed home.

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:07.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think some people
didn't think it was --

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.014 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Like, everybody said --

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:11.584
Even "The New York Times"
on election day in 2016

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:14.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
in that box
where they predict...

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...said that there was only

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:20.727
a "15% chance today"
of Trump winning the presidency.

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:21.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-Okay.

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you got to throw
all that out.

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got to quit this kind of
predicting nonsense,

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you just got to
do your job as a citizen.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody's got to get off
the bench this time.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.171 line:92%
We may not get another time.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:34.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's actually talked about,
you know,

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:37.710
"Well, you know, maybe we'll
have to postpone an election

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.978 line:92%
because there's these --"

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:40.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't do
the voice that you do.

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, you're doing great.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:43.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
This is -- This --

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:43.950 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:47.320
-By the way, you're like the
only person who can't do Trump.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:50.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right?
This is you with a cold.

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:52.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, yeah.
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:55.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But it's -- it's --
People have to --

00:04:55.695 --> 00:05:00.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
look, I think, obviously,
one of two things can happen.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:04.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I heard Steve Bannon
lay out his blueprint

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:06.506
of how they think
they're going to win on Tuesday.

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:11.077
And they think they're gonna
keep the House by one seat.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
And anybody
who doesn't trust that,

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:17.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
please remember that
Donald Trump outsmarted us.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.152 size:88% position:44% line:92%
He outsmarted us in 2016

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:22.755 size:84% position:42%
and won the White House
by losing the election.

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:27.026
That takes a certain kind of
evil genius to figure that out.

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:31.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
So don't think for a second
that, come Tuesday,

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:33.066 line:92%
they don't have every intention

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:35.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
of holding on to the House
and the Senate.

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:38.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they are good
at what they do.

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:41.140 line:92%
And you should respect the fact

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:43.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they are able
to get away with this.

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:46.245 size:81% position:41%
They got away with it
with Gore when he won.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.480 line:92%
We didn't do anything about it.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
They got away with it
when Hillary won.

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:50.683 line:92%
We don't do anything about it.

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
They know us.
-Yeah.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:55.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They know we're busy,
and we got other things to do.

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:56.155 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:59.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But they are fanatical
about this

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they know
their time is up.

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:05.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
And sort of the --
the "angry white guy,"

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:07.300
which, actually,
I'm really Trump's demographic.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. You're a Michigan
angry white guy.

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:12.472
-I'm an angry white guy over 50
with a high school education.

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:13.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So that's me.

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:15.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So if I could just speak

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:18.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
to my fellow angry white
American guys

00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:21.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are semi-uneducated
like me...

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:22.315 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.315 --> 00:06:25.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dudes, give it up!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:28.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've been running the show
for 10,000 years.

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:29.589 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:33.826
It's like --
It's like, we've had a long run

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.128 line:92%
as men running everything.

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:39.499
And, you know, the Yankees
could never win as many pennants

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:41.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
as we've won
in these 10,000 years as men.

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:42.135 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:44.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So why don't we just
take a break?

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let the majority gender
run the show.

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:50.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just for -- yeah.
Just to see how it would go.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.011 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-What are you scared of?

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:53.813 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Women actually like us.

00:06:53.813 --> 00:06:54.847 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.847 --> 00:06:56.282 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Most of us.

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:59.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
So -- So I just think

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:00.586 size:75% position:38% line:92%
there's just this --

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:01.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump is in there
trying to whip up,

00:07:01.988 --> 00:07:04.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
as you were showing earlier,
that all that fear

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all that
"Here come the hordes,"

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:08.060 line:92%
and doing this and that...

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.129 line:92%
It's like, you know, people --

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:15.101
Hopefully, people have not
fallen for it, not the majority.

00:07:15.101 --> 00:07:16.002 line:92%
The majority are with us.

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:19.939 size:81% position:41%
The majority believe
in the liberal agenda.

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:21.240 line:92%
Every poll shows this, Seth.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:24.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whether it's climate change,
equal pay for women,

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:27.880
raising the minimum wage,
the majority of Americans

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
agree with all those things
should happen,

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:34.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we've got to trust that
and start to feel that

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:38.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have the power, but we have
to exercise it on Tuesday.

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:39.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you got
to get five people --

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:43.296
Everyone in here knows five
people that doesn't vote.

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:44.163 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And we've got to get --

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:45.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
bring five people
to the polls with you.

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:49.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have a party afterwards.
Bring beer.

00:07:49.769 --> 00:07:50.803 line:92%
Do whatever you've got to do,

00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:54.540
but let's pack
those polling places on Tuesday.

